hi I'm Evan Carmichael and welcome to  another edition of modeling the Masters  today we're going to look at how a  single mother on welfare followed her  passion for writing and became the first  billion-dollar author and highest  earning novelist in history this is a  story of JK Rowling and the top three  lessons that you can learn from her  success JK Rowling is a British author  best known as a creator of the harry  potter fantasy series rolling was a  single mother living on welfare working  as a secretary was not how she had  envisioned her life she had admittedly  reached her own personal rock bottom  without even enough money to pay the  electricity bill rolling knew she had to  do something to provide a better life  for her and her baby daughter but what  she wondered the answer came to her  while riding the train one day that was  when Harry Potter came to life after  completing the first Harry Potter book  twelve publishers rejected it but number  13 proved to be the lucky one within a  few months Rowling's Harry Potter  character had come to life between the  pages of a book in England a few months  after that the American rights to the  novel were bought for a hefty sum with  that rolling finally quit her teaching  job and decided to focus full-time on  writing today the store is rolling first  wrote in coffee shops have become famous  the world over not only has books but as  movies computer games music and more  she's the world's first billion-dollar  author and the highest earning novelist  in history the Potter books have gained  worldwide attention when multiple awards  sold more than 400 million copies I'm in  the basis for popular series of films in  2007 time magazine named rolling  runner-up for its Person of the Year and  2010 forbes estimated her net worth to  be 1 billion dollars  by following her passion am I never  giving up ruling gut off welfare and  went on to become a billionaire to help  you tap into your passion here are three  action items that you can learn from JK  Rowling action item number one get over  your fear of failure nobody wants to  fail but you can't let the fear of  failing prevent you from making  important decisions in your life  anything that's worth doing will come  with a healthy dose of fear successful  entrepreneurs are the ones who can plow  through that fear and come out  victorious on the other side rolling  couldn't believe the number of different  stories publishing houses gave her  that's why they didn't want to print her  manuscript her story was too long too  fantastical I wouldn't do well selling  to a mainstream audience they said she  remained patient and had faith in her  product she continued to send it out the  publishing houses until she found one  who saw in her story which she did a  success it was one year before the time  rolling finished her first Harry Potter  book to the time that a publisher  finally agreed to buy it and publish it  according to Rolling anything is  possible if you've got enough nerve I  was determined to try I was determined  to try because frankly my life was such  a mess at that point what what was the  worst that could happen everyone turned  me down big deal  action item number two make every second  count you only have so much time today  to get work done and as entrepreneurs we  usually have too many projects on the go  to keep track of it's hard work getting  the business off the ground and you need  to make every second count Harry Potter  came to life on a day that Rowling was  stuck on a train between manchester and  london during the four-hour delay  passenger sitting next to her might have  used the time to catch up on some sleep  but rolling was determined to use time  to her advantage whether it was a  15-minute break from her secretarial  duties at Amnesty International or 30  minute nap time break from her baby  daughter Rowland used every spare second  to dream up and jot down points for her  story according to Rolling where the  idea of Harry Potter actually came from  I really couldn't tell you I was  traveling on a train between manchester  and london and it just popped into my  head i spent four hours thinking about  what hogwarts would look like the most  interesting train journey I've ever  taken by the time I got off at Kings  Cross many of the characters in the  books had already been invented  action item number three love what you  do if you don't love what you do you're  not going to have much success as an  entrepreneur you're going to quit as  soon as it gets tough and you're not  going to make a meaningful contribution  to your community as with all matters of  the heart you'll know it's right when  you find it rolling wanted to make your  contribution to the world to add her  unique something that nobody else could  bring to the table and that unique  something was her writing she never went  searching for the kind of success that  she's received today she simply wanted  to do best but she loved most and that  was writing putting the rolling I just  write what I wanted to write I write  what amuses me it's totally for myself  I'm an extremely lucky person doing what  I love best in the world I'm sure that  I'll always be a writer  so remember get over your fear of  failure make every second count and love  what you do to finish up this video I  wanted to share one of my favorite true  stories of JK Rowling and some of her  best quotes Harry Potter was not an  instant success in fact at the very  first book reading rolling did for her  first Harry Potter novel only four  people showed up to hear her the staff  of the bookstore felt so sorry for her  that they stood around and listen to  Roland's editor then advised her to get  a day job since she had little chance of  ever making money in children's books  thank you for joining me for another  edition of modern masters if you enjoyed  the video please give it a thumbs up and  also love to hear your comments if you  leave some feedback below the video and  stay tuned for the next episode
 

